Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:45:38 +0100
Subject: NIFI-16547 Add connect timeout to cluster protocol sockets

SocketUtils.createSocket connected via new Socket(host, port) and SSLSocketFactory.createSocket(host, port), so connect() had no timeout and blocked for the OS TCP connect timeout (~127 s on Linux) against peers that silently drop packets, e.g. the old IP of a restarted Kubernetes pod. This stalled heartbeats, the coordinator heartbeat monitor and /health/cluster.

Changes in this commit:
- Create an unconnected socket and connect with a timeout. The hostname is still resolved on every attempt and kept for TLS hostname verification.
- Add connectTimeout to SocketConfiguration, set from nifi.cluster.node.connection.timeout for the cluster protocol.
- Treat a connect timeout like a ConnectException when notifying the subject node of a status change, so it is not retried 5 times on the heartbeat monitor thread.
